(7644334, 1241930, 112739, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Roz! I thought this image was executed very well, but I was really wanting to see some color in the details and the bokeh. What caused you to enter a B&amp;W entry? Just curious...</td>', 'Congratulations Roz! I thought this image was executed very well, but I was really wanting to see some color in the details and the bokeh. What caused you to enter a B&W entry? Just curious...', '2019-10-22 16:53:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7644359, 1241930, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dennisheckman:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations Roz! I thought this image was executed very well, but I was really wanting to see some color in the details and the bokeh. What caused you to enter a B&amp;W entry? Just curious... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks for your comment Dennis .. :)<br/>to answer your question .. I LOVE BLACK AND WHITE .. !! .. <br/>plus my monitor needs calibrating .. i can never be totally confident that the colours i see on my pc are the same as those seen by other people .. i usually check on my phone and laptop to see what the colours look like .. and usually on the phone they are much more saturated .. especially the red .. and on the laptop they are more subdued .. i''m using windows 7 on the pc and windows 10 on the laptop .. my phone is samsung s9+ .. <br/>anyway .. during the editing process i did consider this in colour ..  but i felt it had much more impact in black and white .. :)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Dennisheckman: Congratulations Roz! I thought this image was executed very well, but I was really wanting to see some color in the details and the bokeh. What caused you to enter a B&W entry? Just curious...   thanks for your comment Dennis .. :)to answer your question .. I LOVE BLACK AND WHITE .. !! .. plus my monitor needs calibrating .. i can never be totally confident that the colours i see on my pc are the same as those seen by other people .. i usually check on my phone and laptop to see what the colours look like .. and usually on the phone they are much more saturated .. especially the red .. and on the laptop they are more subdued .. i''m using windows 7 on the pc and windows 10 on the laptop .. my phone is samsung s9+ .. anyway .. during the editing process i did consider this in colour ..  but i felt it had much more impact in black and white .. :)', '2019-10-22 21:11:36.000000', NULL, 0),
